\newlabel{fig:cds_cashflows}{{33.1}{423}{CDS cashflow structure. The protection \emph {buyer} pays quarterly premiums $s\,\delta _i$ per unit notional (blue arrows, upward) at each scheduled date, but only while the reference entity survives. If default occurs at $\tau $, the protection \emph {seller} pays $(1-R)N$ (red dashed arrow, downward) and all further premium payments stop. The par spread $s^*$ is set so these two legs have equal present value at inception}{figure.33.1}{}}
