\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {35.1}{\ignorespaces Three-period CRR binomial tree. At each step the price moves up by factor $u = e^{\sigma \sqrt  {\Delta t}}$ or down by $d = 1/u$, with risk-neutral probability $p = (e^{r\Delta t} - d)/(u - d)$. The recombining property ($ud = du = S_0$) means the tree has $N+1$ terminal nodes after $N$ steps, not $2^N$. Option prices are obtained by \emph  {backward induction}: compute payoffs at $t=3$, then take risk-neutral expectations one step at a time back to $t=0$.}}{459}{figure.35.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:binomial_tree}{{35.1}{459}{Three-period CRR binomial tree. At each step the price moves up by factor $u = e^{\sigma \sqrt {\Delta t}}$ or down by $d = 1/u$, with risk-neutral probability $p = (e^{r\Delta t} - d)/(u - d)$. The recombining property ($ud = du = S_0$) means the tree has $N+1$ terminal nodes after $N$ steps, not $2^N$. Option prices are obtained by \emph {backward induction}: compute payoffs at $t=3$, then take risk-neutral expectations one step at a time back to $t=0$}{figure.35.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:binomial_tree@cref}{{[figure][1][35]35.1}{[1][458][]459}{}{}{}}
